{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1494147-initiative-in-trinity-2e","id":1494147,"title":"Initiative in Trinity 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-02T12:55:49-07:00","id":1494147,"title":"Initiative in Trinity 2E","content":"So, I run first battle using <b>TC Core</b> rules - and was totally baffled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TC Core, page 101</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each player rolls the lower of Athletics + Cunning or Empathy + Dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand using <i>Athletics + Cunning</i> easily - <b>but WHY <i>Empathy+Dexterity</i> pool?</b>\ud83d\ude2e How it should even work? Can someone describe it to me?<br /> <br /> As house rule, I will probably go with <b>Scion</b> 2E interpretation of Imitative to our games:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scion 2E Origin, page 115</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character\u2019s initiative pool is equal to the character\u2019s best combat-related Skill + Cunning. This pool represents a character\u2019s martial acumen and mental presence in the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>( With Athletics being alternative to other combat-related Skills to use here. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T13:45:33-07:00","id":1494151,"title":"","content":"Your pool is based on combining how fast you can move with how good you are at reacting to others.<br /> <br /> So you need either the Attribute or Skill for moving fast (Dexterity or Athletics)<br /> <br /> And either the Attribute or Skill for reacting to others (Cunning or Empathy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T14:11:59-07:00","id":1494154,"title":"","content":"What glamourweaver said.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd be careful with importing rules from Scion. While the Scion rule is fine if you're running base-line humans or Talents in TC, once you start getting into Novas and Psi, TC uses a much more delineated approach to a few things. It's meant to be a more set instance of the Storypath rules, rather than a more off-the-cuff one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T18:45:37-07:00","id":1494168,"title":"","content":"I use the Trinity rule, but I don't require my players to use the lower of the two pools. That was a fine rule for a horror game like nWoD, but it seems like an unnecessary limitation for a game that is intended to be a competence fantasy like Trinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T02:54:51-07:00","id":1494191,"title":"","content":"Honestly, using the lower will level the problem and in general I would recommend to use the Desperation pool for Antagonists.<br /> <br /> It keeps the number of dice low and value the characters with powers that deal with this, and I think there is at least one for each template.<br /> Also, as the order only defines which team will act, not the order of the characters, it can be really irrelevant to have a large pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T05:12:33-07:00","id":1494204,"title":"","content":"I find that diversitying the pool gives me a wider range of values rolled, so I don't need rolls offs to set where the slots are. Otherwise everyone usually rolls between 0-2 and so most of the slots end up with the same number. Also, on a psychological level, allowing the player to roll a slightly larger pool increases the feeling of power and ability. Using the larger of the two pools just feels more fun to my players, but your milage may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T09:49:48-07:00","id":1494225,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'm not sure I'd even roll for initiative, just start with whoever makes sense at the time and continue from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T10:13:08-07:00","id":1494228,"title":"","content":"Rolling the higher of the two feels better, but it also encourages people to choose a few traits and pump them up, while the rest of the system encourages you to take a broader approach to distributing your dots. Specialties are meant to encourage you to focus on a broader skill set, for example. Requiring the lower of those two pools also encourages you to diversify your dots. I like that personally. It was certainly a paradigm shift for my players coming off a V20 game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T03:00:00-07:00","id":1494717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1494147-initiative-in-trinity-2e?p=1494204#post1494204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that diversitying the pool gives me a wider range of values rolled, so I don't need rolls offs to set where the slots are. Otherwise everyone usually rolls between 0-2 and so most of the slots end up with the same number. Also, on a psychological level, allowing the player to roll a slightly larger pool increases the feeling of power and ability. Using the larger of the two pools just feels more fun to my players, but your milage may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is true, the range is very short.<br /> Sometimes I use a house rule: Roll one die and add the initiative bonus.<br /> It's faster and gives a larger range, but the initiative bonuses become less powerful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T05:34:18-07:00","id":1494723,"title":"","content":"To reiterate though, once you get past base-line humans and low-to-mid power Talents, the system gets very different very fast. Once characters start getting much more regular access to 3+ worth of enhancements and/or Scale that can apply to initiative, that &quot;everyone ends up in the 0-2 range&quot; stops being then normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}